vulgure or sleeper witness it. I think I am confuseing myself or over reading the section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you using the first edition or the second edition?<br /> <br /> In very brief:<br /> <br /> First Edition: There are two kinds of spells: <i>vulgar </i>and <i>coincidental</i>. If you cast a vulgar spell (a spell where a hypothetical viewer would say, &quot;That's magic!&quot;) you incur Paradox. Sleepers make Paradox worse, but don't provoke it in and of themselves. The base dice pool for Paradox is determined by your Gnosis, plus circumstantial modifiers, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> Second Edition: The dice pool for Paradox is, again, a number set by the mage's Gnosis, multiplied by the number of extra Reach the character spends beyond what they get for &quot;free&quot; -- that is, Reach that can be spent freely without risking Paradox. Sleepers invoke Paradox (or can make it worse) when they see obvious Supernal magic, but there's no distinction between <i>vulgar </i>and <i>coincidental</i>. Mages can cast the most whacked out, obvious magic and not have the Lie zap them for it, provided they don't exceed their Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:18:28-07:00","id":983414,"title":"","content":"There is no such thing as vulgar spells in second edition. If an effect of a spell is obviously magical and there are one or more Sleeper witnesses, the Storyteller adds one die to the Paradox dice pool (and gets 9-again if there are small handful of Sleeper witnesses, 8-again if there is a group of them, or Rote quality if there is a large crowd of them). If the Mage uses more Reach than the free Reach granted by her rating in the spell's primary Arcanum, the Storyteller adds a number of dice to the Paradox dice pool, determined by the Mage's Gnosis, per Reach over the limit. If the Mage has Innured the spell they are casting, the Storyteller adds two dice to the Paradox dice pool. If there are any dice in the Paradox dice pool, for any of these reasons, there is a chance of Paradox. The Mage can use their Dedicated magical tool as a Yantra to remove two dice from the Storyteller's pool, and spend mana to remove dice from the Storyteller's pool on a 1-for-1 basis, but even if they reduce the pool to 0 dice, the Storyteller still rolls a chance die. What the Paradox does is determined by how many successes the Storyteller rolls on the Paradox dice pool, and if the Mage Contained or Released the Paradox. Once the Storyteller has rolled for Paradox, they get one more Paradox die on all subsequent Paradox dice pools in the same scene, and this effect is cumulative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-07-2016, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}